<title>SWITZERLAND: Wella details nine-month results.</title>
<headline>Wella details nine-month results.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wella AG, the German haircare and cosmetics company, said that its pre-tax group profit in the nine months ended September 30 fell to 84.4 million marks ($56.2 million) from 88.1 million in the previous nine-month period.</p>
<p>But it said it expected a significantly better operating result, and a slightly higher pre-tax earnings figure for the year.</p>
<p>It also said that it expected sales revenue to be up by seven to 10 percent.</p>
<p>Its profit, unlike last year, contained no extraordinary items. In the previous year, it said that its pre-tax profit was 144 million marks, with about 35 million reflecting funds which were no longer needed for provisions.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340 ($ = 1.502 German Marks)</p>
